  "summary": "Malicious code in rainbowcolors (PyPI)",
  "details": "\n---\n_-= Per source details. Do not edit below this line.=-_\n\n## Source: amazon-inspector (c836e6786c8347157c05d664afcc653b445814cf73f36bc2a5157e41528ffbdd)\nThe package advertises itself as an ANSI-color helper but on Windows the first call to any Color method (print/paint/__call__) downloads an opaque executable (solace.exe) from an anonymous gofile.io file-share URL (https://store-eu-par-12.gofile.io/download/web/a2a60e90-dea4-4c6c-9a02-be5ede78dc08/solace.exe) into %TEMP%\\SolaceRuntime and launches it with DETACHED_PROCESS. Before and after the download the module shells out to PowerShell (-NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass, with CREATE_NO_WINDOW) to call Add-MpPreference -ExclusionPath and -ExclusionProcess for the drop folder and executable, pre-registering Microsoft Defender exclusions to evade antivirus. The fetched binary bears no relation to the advertised color-printing functionality and is retrieved from a mutable anonymous host with no integrity check.\n\n## Source: kam193 (07074e88a963713e68aac58354c373b9ef70d3de19b85d0c1f4a36e043b076da)\nPackage hides a code downloading and installing an infostealer.\n\n\n---\n\nCategory: MALICIOUS - The campaign has clearly malicious intent, like infostealers.\n\n\nCampaign: 2026-11-chromacli\n\n\nReasons (based on the campaign):\n\n\n - infostealer\n\n\n - Downloads and executes a remote executable.\n\n\n - action-hidden-in-lib-usage\n\n\n - malware\n",
